{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'curl -fsSL https://qrypt-quickstart.pages.dev/'","aggregated_output":"<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1\"><title>Qrypt quantum entropy quickstart: AES-256 key in 5 minutes</title><meta name=\"description\" content=\"Get an AES-256-GCM key from Qrypt quantum entropy in about 5 minutes with Python or Node.\"><link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/style.css\"><link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/highlight.css\"></head><body>\n<a class=\"skip\" href=\"#main\">Skip to content</a><header><nav aria-label=\"Site\"><a href=\"/\">Quickstart</a><a href=\"/troubleshooting\">Troubleshooting</a><a href=\"/llms.txt\">llms.txt</a></nav></header><main id=\"main\">\n<h1>Make an AES-256 key from quantum entropy</h1>\n<aside class=\"agent-note\" aria-label=\"Note for AI coding agents\"><p><strong>AI coding agents, read this first:</strong> never read, print or dump <code>.env</code> or environment variables, and never ask the human to paste the token into chat. Ask them to create <code>.env</code> themselves and confirm it is set. If <code>QRYPT-ISOLATED.txt</code> exists you have no token on purpose: run mock tests and ask the human to run <code>agent-sandbox/verify.sh</code> on the host. Full rules: <a href=\"#quick-setup\">Quick Setup</a> and <a href=\"/llms.txt\">llms.txt</a>.</p></aside>\n\n<p><span class=\"time\">Time target: about 5 minutes</span> No SDK needed: one HTTPS GET, then standard crypto.</p>\n<h2>1. Get a token</h2>\n<p>Create an account at <a href=\"https://portal.qrypt.com/register\">portal.qrypt.com/register</a> and generate a token for the <strong>Entropy</strong> service. It is shown only once and is billed like a password: keep it secret.</p>\n<h2>2. Save it in <code>.env</code></h2>\n<div class=\"codebox\"><button class=\"copy\" data-target=\"c-env\" aria-label=\"Copy .env line\">Copy</button><pre class=\"hl\" tabindex=\"0\"><code id=\"c-env\" data-lang=\"env\"><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"nv\">QRYPT_API_KEY</span><span class=\"o\">=</span>paste-your-token-here</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>Put <code>.env</code> next to the script and add it to <code>.gitignore</code>. Never print it, not even partly (no <code>cat .env</code>). To check the file exists, run <code>test -f .env &amp;&amp; echo set</code>.</p>\n<h2>3. Run the snippet</h2>\n<div role=\"tablist\" aria-label=\"Language\">\n<button role=\"tab\" id=\"t-py\" aria-selected=\"true\" aria-controls=\"p-py\">Python</button>\n<button role=\"tab\" id=\"t-js\" aria-selected=\"false\" aria-controls=\"p-js\" tabindex=\"-1\">Node</button></div>\n<section role=\"tabpanel\" id=\"p-py\" aria-labelledby=\"t-py\" tabindex=\"0\">\n<p>Python 3.9+. Uses <code>requests</code>: Cloudflare blocks Python's built-in <code>urllib</code> User-Agent.</p>\n<div class=\"codebox\"><button class=\"copy\" data-target=\"c-pyi\" aria-label=\"Copy Python install command\">Copy</button><pre class=\"hl\" tabindex=\"0\"><code id=\"c-pyi\" data-lang=\"bash\"><span class=\"line\">python3<span class=\"w\"> </span>-m<span class=\"w\"> </span>venv<span class=\"w\"> </span>.venv<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&amp;&amp;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span>.venv/bin/pip<span class=\"w\"> </span>install<span class=\"w\"> </span>requests<span class=\"w\"> </span>cryptography<span class=\"w\"> </span>python-dotenv</span></code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"codebox\"><button class=\"copy\" data-target=\"c-py\" aria-label=\"Copy Python quickstart code\">Copy</button><pre class=\"hl\" tabindex=\"0\"><code id=\"c-py\" data-lang=\"python\" class=\"numbered\"><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"c1\"># Qrypt quickstart (Python): 1 KiB of quantum entropy -&gt; AES-256-GCM key.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"c1\"># Setup: pip install requests cryptography python-dotenv</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"c1\"># Then put QRYPT_API_KEY=[REDACTED] token&gt; in a .env file next to this script.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">base64</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">os</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">sys</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">requests</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"kn\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">cryptography.hazmat.primitives.ciphers.aead</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span> <span class=\"n\">AESGCM</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"kn\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">dotenv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span> <span class=\"n\">load_dotenv</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"n\">API</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">os</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getenv</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;QRYPT_BASE_URL&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"s2\">&quot;https://api-eus.qrypt.com&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>  <span class=\"c1\"># mock override</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"c1\"># One friendly message per failure. We never retry automatically.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"n\">HELP</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"kc\">None</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"s2\">&quot;QRYPT_API_KEY is missing: add it to .env (see .env.example).&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\">        <span class=\"mi\">400</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"s2\">&quot;400: size must be 1-512. It counts KiB, not bytes.&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\">        <span class=\"mi\">401</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"s2\">&quot;401: Authorization header missing, malformed or expired.&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\">        <span class=\"mi\">403</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"s2\">&quot;403: Token invalid OR monthly quota used. Check the token first.&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\">        <span class=\"mi\">429</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"s2\">&quot;429: rate limited. Live can return 429 about 1 s after a single &quot;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\">             <span class=\"s2\">&quot;prior call; wait 10 s or more and never loop.&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">}</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"c1\"># 500, 503 and anything else: Qrypt is busy or erroring, so try again later.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"c1\"># Step 1: read the token from .env. Never print or log it.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"n\">load_dotenv</span><span class=\"p\">()</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"n\">token</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">os</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getenv</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;QRYPT_API_KEY&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"ow\">or</span> <span class=\"n\">sys</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">exit</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">HELP</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"kc\">None</span><span class=\"p\">])</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"c1\"># Step 2: fetch 1 KiB of entropy. A custom User-Agent avoids Cloudflare&#39;s</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"c1\"># block on Python&#39;s urllib; X-Qrypt-Client tags quickstart traffic.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"n\">headers</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"p\">{</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\">    <span class=\"s2\">&quot;Authorization&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;Bearer </span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">token</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"s2\">&quot;Accept&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"s2\">&quot;application/json&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\">    <span class=\"s2\">&quot;User-Agent&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"s2\">&quot;qrypt-quickstart/1.0&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"s2\">&quot;X-Qrypt-Client&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"s2\">&quot;quickstart-py/1.0&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">}</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"k\">try</span><span class=\"p\">:</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\">    <span class=\"n\">resp</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">requests</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">get</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">API</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s2\">/api/v1/quantum-entropy&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">params</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;size&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">},</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\">                        <span class=\"n\">headers</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"n\">headers</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">timeout</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"mi\">15</span><span class=\"p\">)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\">    <span class=\"k\">if</span> <span class=\"n\">resp</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">status_code</span> <span class=\"o\">!=</span> <span class=\"mi\">200</span><span class=\"p\">:</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\">        <span class=\"n\">sys</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">exit</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">HELP</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">get</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">resp</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">status_code</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">resp</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">status_code</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s2\">: Qrypt is &quot;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\">                          <span class=\"s2\">&quot;busy or erroring. Try again shortly.&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">))</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\">    <span class=\"n\">entropy_b64</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">resp</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">json</span><span class=\"p\">()[</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;random&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">][</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"k\">except</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">requests</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">RequestException</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"ne\">ValueError</span><span class=\"p\">):</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\">    <span class=\"n\">sys</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">exit</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;Network error or non-JSON reply: check proxy/TLS, retry soon.&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"c1\"># Step 3: decode first, then keep 32 bytes as the AES-256 key.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"n\">key</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">base64</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">b64decode</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">entropy_b64</span><span class=\"p\">)[:</span><span class=\"mi\">32</span><span class=\"p\">]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"c1\"># Step 4: encrypt and decrypt a sample message with AES-256-GCM.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"n\">aes</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">nonce</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">message</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">AESGCM</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">key</span><span class=\"p\">),</span> <span class=\"n\">os</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">urandom</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">12</span><span class=\"p\">),</span> <span class=\"sa\">b</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;hello, quantum entropy&quot;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"k\">assert</span> <span class=\"n\">aes</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">decrypt</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">nonce</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">aes</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">encrypt</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">nonce</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">message</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"kc\">None</span><span class=\"p\">),</span> <span class=\"kc\">None</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"o\">==</span> <span class=\"n\">message</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"nb\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;Success: AES-256-GCM round trip with a Qrypt key (not shown).&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">)</span></span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"codebox\"><button class=\"copy\" data-target=\"c-pyr\" aria-label=\"Copy Python run command\">Copy</button><pre class=\"hl\" tabindex=\"0\"><code id=\"c-pyr\" data-lang=\"bash\"><span class=\"line\">.venv/bin/python<span class=\"w\"> </span>quickstart.py</span></code></pre></div></section>\n<section role=\"tabpanel\" id=\"p-js\" aria-labelledby=\"t-js\" tabindex=\"0\" hidden>\n<p>Node 20.12+ (built-in <code>fetch</code> and <code>process.loadEnvFile</code>). No dependencies.</p>\n<div class=\"codebox\"><button class=\"copy\" data-target=\"c-js\" aria-label=\"Copy Node quickstart code\">Copy</button><pre class=\"hl\" tabindex=\"0\"><code id=\"c-js\" data-lang=\"js\" class=\"numbered\"><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"c1\">// Qrypt quickstart (Node 20.12+): 1 KiB of quantum entropy -&gt; AES-256-GCM key.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"c1\">// No dependencies. Put QRYPT_API_KEY=[REDACTED] token&gt; in a .env file here.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"k\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">assert</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kr\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;node:assert&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"k\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">existsSync</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kr\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;node:fs&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"k\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">createCipheriv</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">createDecipheriv</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">randomBytes</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kr\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;node:crypto&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"kd\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">API</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">process</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">env</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">QRYPT_BASE_URL</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">??</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;https://api-eus.qrypt.com&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">// mock</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"c1\">// One friendly message per failure. We never retry automatically.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"kd\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">HELP</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">missing</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;QRYPT_API_KEY is missing: add it to .env.&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"nx\">network</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;Network error or non-JSON reply: check proxy/TLS, retry soon.&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"mf\">400</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;400: size must be 1-512. It counts KiB, not bytes.&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"mf\">401</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;401: Authorization header missing, malformed or expired.&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"mf\">403</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;403: Token invalid OR monthly quota used. Check the token first.&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"mf\">429</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;429: rate limited. Live can return 429 about 1 s after a single &quot;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;prior call; wait 10 s or more and never loop.&quot;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">};</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"c1\">// 500, 503 and anything else: Qrypt is busy or erroring, so try again later.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"kd\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">fail</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">msg</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">console</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">error</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">msg</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">process</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">exit</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mf\">1</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">};</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"c1\">// Step 1: read the token from .env. Never print or log it.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">existsSync</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;.env&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">process</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">loadEnvFile</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;.env&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"kd\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">token</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">process</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">env</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">QRYPT_API_KEY</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">||</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">fail</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">HELP</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">missing</span><span class=\"p\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"c1\">// Step 2: fetch 1 KiB of entropy (size counts KiB, not bytes).</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"kd\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">headers</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Authorization</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"sb\">`Bearer </span><span class=\"si\">${</span><span class=\"nx\">token</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"sb\">`</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Accept</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;application/json&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;User-Agent&quot;</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;qrypt-quickstart/1.0&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;X-Qrypt-Client&quot;</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;quickstart-js/1.0&quot;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">};</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"kd\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">url</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"sb\">`</span><span class=\"si\">${</span><span class=\"nx\">API</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"sb\">/api/v1/quantum-entropy?size=1`</span><span class=\"p\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"kd\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">res</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">await</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">fetch</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">url</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">headers</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}).</span><span class=\"k\">catch</span><span class=\"p\">(()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">fail</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">HELP</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">network</span><span class=\"p\">));</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">res</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">status</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">!==</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">200</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">fail</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">HELP</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nx\">res</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">status</span><span class=\"p\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">??</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"sb\">`</span><span class=\"si\">${</span><span class=\"nx\">res</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">status</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"sb\">: Qrypt is busy or erroring. Try again shortly.`</span><span class=\"p\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"kd\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">body</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">await</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">res</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">json</span><span class=\"p\">().</span><span class=\"k\">catch</span><span class=\"p\">(()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">fail</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">HELP</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">network</span><span class=\"p\">));</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"c1\">// Step 3: decode first, then keep 32 bytes as the AES-256 key.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"kd\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">key</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Buffer</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"kr\">from</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">body</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">random</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"mf\">0</span><span class=\"p\">],</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;base64&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">).</span><span class=\"nx\">subarray</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mf\">0</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">32</span><span class=\"p\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"c1\">// Step 4: encrypt and decrypt a sample message with AES-256-GCM.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"kd\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">GCM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;aes-256-gcm&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">iv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">randomBytes</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mf\">12</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">message</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;hello, quantum&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"kd\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">enc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">createCipheriv</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">GCM</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">key</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">iv</span><span class=\"p\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"kd\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">sealed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Buffer</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">concat</span><span class=\"p\">([</span><span class=\"nx\">enc</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">update</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">message</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;utf8&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">enc</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"kr\">final</span><span class=\"p\">()]);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"kd\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">dec</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">createDecipheriv</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">GCM</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">key</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">iv</span><span class=\"p\">).</span><span class=\"nx\">setAuthTag</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">enc</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">getAuthTag</span><span class=\"p\">());</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"nx\">assert</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">equal</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">dec</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">update</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">sealed</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">null</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;utf8&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">dec</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"kr\">final</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;utf8&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">message</span><span class=\"p\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"nx\">console</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">log</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;Success: AES-256-GCM round trip with a Qrypt key (not shown).&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">);</span></span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"codebox\"><button class=\"copy\" data-target=\"c-jsr\" aria-label=\"Copy Node run command\">Copy</button><pre class=\"hl\" tabindex=\"0\"><code id=\"c-jsr\" data-lang=\"bash\"><span class=\"line\">node<span class=\"w\"> </span>quickstart.mjs</span></code></pre></div></section>\n<h2>What the API returns</h2>\n<p>One base64 string per KiB requested. Decode it before use; it never contains the key itself.</p>\n<pre class=\"hl\" tabindex=\"0\"><code data-lang=\"json\"><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"p\">{</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"nt\">&quot;random&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;&lt;base64 string: 1,024 random bytes when decoded&gt;&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">],</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"nt\">&quot;size&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"p\">}</span></span></code></pre>\n<h2>4. Expected output</h2>\n<pre class=\"hl\" tabindex=\"0\"><code data-lang=\"text\"><span class=\"line\">Success: AES-256-GCM round trip with a Qrypt key (not shown).</span></code></pre>\n<h2>Things that trip people up</h2>\n<ul><li><code>size</code> counts <strong>KiB</strong>, not bytes. Ask for <code>size=1</code> (1,024 bytes) and take 32 bytes.</li>\n<li>Base64-decode the string first; never use the text itself as the key.</li>\n<li>Live can return 429 about 1 s after a single prior call; wait 10 s or more and never loop.</li>\n<li>A wrong token returns <strong>403</strong>, the same as an exhausted quota. Check the token first.</li>\n<li>Never print, log or commit the key or token. Use fresh entropy for each key.</li></ul>\n<p>Errors? See <a href=\"/troubleshooting\">Troubleshooting</a>.</p>\n<section aria-labelledby=\"h-agent\">\n<h2 id=\"h-agent\">Using an AI coding agent?</h2>\n<p>Two modes. <strong>Quick Setup is the default</strong> (no Docker). Isolated Setup is optional when you want stronger credential boundaries.</p>\n\n<table class=\"cmp\"><caption>Quick Setup vs Isolated Setup</caption>\n<thead><tr><th scope=\"col\"></th><th scope=\"col\">Quick Setup (default)</th><th scope=\"col\">Isolated Setup</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><th scope=\"row\">Best for</th><td>Trying the API in under 10 minutes with Claude Code, Codex, Cursor or similar</td><td>Repos that already hold secrets, or any run where the agent must not see credentials</td></tr>\n<tr><th scope=\"row\">Docker required</th><td>No</td><td>Yes</td></tr>\n<tr><th scope=\"row\">Agent can access existing project secrets</th><td>Yes — unrestricted agents can read files, including <code>.env</code></td><td>No — project must not contain <code>.env</code>; host secrets stay off the mount</td></tr>\n<tr><th scope=\"row\">Credential exposure risk</th><td>Behavioral only. Agents may log file contents. Use a disposable token.</td><td>Token never enters the agent container. Live verify runs fixed snippets on the host.</td></tr>\n<tr><th scope=\"row\">Human credential setup</th><td>You create <code>.env</code> yourself; never paste the token into chat</td><td>You keep <code>.env</code> outside the project (e.g. <code>~/.config/qrypt/.env</code>)</td></tr>\n<tr><th scope=\"row\">Live verification</th><td>Agent runs the example after you confirm <code>.env</code> is set</td><td>You run <code>agent-sandbox/verify.sh --env …</code> (sanitized PASS/FAIL only)</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\n<details open id=\"quick-setup\">\n<summary><strong>Option A — Quick Setup</strong> (default, no Docker)</summary>\n<div class=\"warn\" role=\"note\">\n<p><strong>Security warning.</strong> AI coding agents may access files containing credentials, including existing <code>.env</code> files, before reading these instructions. Credential values could appear in agent session logs. For this quick setup, use disposable API credentials where possible and rotate any credentials that were exposed or may have been compromised. For stronger protection, choose Isolated Setup.</p>\n</div>\n<ol>\n<li>Paste this prompt into Claude Code, Codex, Cursor or another coding agent:\n<div class=\"codebox\"><button class=\"copy\" data-target=\"c-prompt\" aria-label=\"Copy Quick Setup agent prompt\">Copy</button>\n<pre class=\"hl\" tabindex=\"0\"><code id=\"c-prompt\" data-lang=\"text\"><span class=\"line\">Quickstart: https://qrypt-quickstart.pages.dev/  (also /llms.txt)</span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\">Goal: AES-256-GCM round trip using 1 KiB of Qrypt quantum entropy.</span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\">Rules (follow all of them):</span>\n<span class=\"line\">- Read the quickstart and pick Python or Node (ask me if unsure).</span>\n<span class=\"line\">- Use the official snippets from the quickstart. Do not invent an SDK.</span>\n<span class=\"line\">- Install dependencies and run the mocked tests first (no real token).</span>\n<span class=\"line\">- NEVER ask me to paste QRYPT_API_KEY into chat, a prompt, CLI args or source.</span>\n<span class=\"line\">- NEVER read, print, cat, head, or dump .env or environment variables.</span>\n<span class=\"line\">- NEVER enable verbose HTTP logging that would log Authorization headers.</span>\n<span class=\"line\">- Ask me to create .env myself (QRYPT_API_KEY=...) and confirm when it is set.</span>\n<span class=\"line\">- After I confirm, run the example. Keep the key in memory only (no key files).</span>\n<span class=\"line\">- If you read .env or a credential by accident, stop and tell me so I can rotate it.</span>\n<span class=\"line\">- Report success with the success line only. Never display the token, entropy or key.</span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\">Security reminder for me at the end: review this agent session for credential exposure and rotate any exposed or potentially compromised API credentials, including unrelated project credentials. Rotating the Qrypt token alone does not protect other secrets.</span></code></pre></div></li>\n<li>The agent reads the quickstart, picks a language, implements with the official snippets and runs the mock tests.</li>\n<li>When asked, create <code>.env</code> yourself (never paste the token into the chat):\n<div class=\"codebox\"><button class=\"copy\" data-target=\"c-env2\" aria-label=\"Copy .env example line\">Copy</button>\n<pre class=\"hl\" tabindex=\"0\"><code id=\"c-env2\" data-lang=\"env\"><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"nv\">QRYPT_API_KEY</span><span class=\"o\">=</span>paste-your-token-here</span></code></pre></div>\nTell the agent only that it is set. Do not share the value.</li>\n<li>The agent runs the example (1 KiB → 32-byte AES-256 key → AES-GCM round trip) and reports the success line without displaying secrets.</li>\n</ol>\n<p class=\"warn\"><strong>End-of-workflow reminder:</strong> Review your agent session for potential credential exposure. Rotate any exposed or potentially compromised API credentials, including unrelated project credentials. Rotating the Qrypt token alone does not protect other secrets.</p>\n<p>These rules are defense-in-depth, not enforceable isolation. Rotation does not make an earlier exposure harmless, and nothing here claims a no-logging guarantee. Prefer Isolated Setup when that matters.</p>\n</details>\n\n<details id=\"isolated-setup\">\n<summary><strong>Option B — Isolated Setup</strong> (Docker; agent never sees the token)</summary>\n<p>The agent runs in a container with <strong>no</strong> <code>.env</code>, no host home, no SSH keys, no cloud credentials and no Docker socket. Live verification is a separate host-side step that runs <em>fixed</em> snippets from this repo — never agent-modifiable code — with the real token.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Download the sandbox into one folder: <a href=\"/agent-sandbox/Dockerfile\">Dockerfile</a>, <a href=\"/agent-sandbox/run.sh\">run.sh</a>, <a href=\"/agent-sandbox/verify.sh\">verify.sh</a>, <a href=\"/agent-sandbox/test-isolation.sh\">test-isolation.sh</a>, <a href=\"/agent-sandbox/README.md\">README.md</a>. Then <code>chmod +x agent-sandbox/*.sh</code>.</li>\n<li>Keep the token <em>outside</em> the project the agent will see:\n<div class=\"codebox\"><button class=\"copy\" data-target=\"c-iso-env\" aria-label=\"Copy isolated env setup commands\">Copy</button>\n<pre class=\"hl\" tabindex=\"0\"><code id=\"c-iso-env\" data-lang=\"bash\"><span class=\"line\">mkdir<span class=\"w\"> </span>-p<span class=\"w\"> </span>~/.config/qrypt</span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"c1\"># put QRYPT_API_KEY=... in ~/.config/qrypt/.env, then:</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\">chmod<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">600</span><span class=\"w\"> </span>~/.config/qrypt/.env</span></code></pre></div></li>\n<li>Start the agent against a clean project directory (must not contain <code>.env</code> — <code>run.sh</code> refuses otherwise):\n<div class=\"codebox\"><button class=\"copy\" data-target=\"c-iso-run\" aria-label=\"Copy isolated run command\">Copy</button>\n<pre class=\"hl\" tabindex=\"0\"><code id=\"c-iso-run\" data-lang=\"bash\"><span class=\"line\">agent-sandbox/run.sh<span class=\"w\"> </span>~/qrypt-demo<span class=\"w\"> </span>your-agent-command</span></code></pre></div></li>\n<li>Inside the container the agent implements the example and runs mock tests. It has no token.</li>\n<li>On the host, after the agent finishes, run trusted verification:\n<div class=\"codebox\"><button class=\"copy\" data-target=\"c-iso-verify\" aria-label=\"Copy verify command\">Copy</button>\n<pre class=\"hl\" tabindex=\"0\"><code id=\"c-iso-verify\" data-lang=\"bash\"><span class=\"line\">agent-sandbox/verify.sh<span class=\"w\"> </span>--env<span class=\"w\"> </span>~/.config/qrypt/.env</span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"c1\"># -&gt; verify python: PASS (AES-GCM round trip; key not shown)</span></span></code></pre></div></li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Honesty about isolation:</strong> this blocks the common failure mode (agents reading <code>.env</code>). It does <em>not</em> claim Docker guarantees zero leakage. A malicious <code>SANDBOX_DOCKER_ARGS</code> that remounts your home directory, a compromised agent binary, or a container escape is out of scope. The boundaries we <em>do</em> claim are checked by <code>agent-sandbox/test-isolation.sh</code>.</p>\n</details>\n</section>\n\n<p id=\"copy-status\" class=\"sr\" aria-live=\"polite\"></p></main><footer><p>Unofficial quickstart. API reference: <a href=\"https://docs.qrypt.com/eaas/\">docs.qrypt.com/eaas</a>. No analytics or cookies.</p></footer>\n<script src=\"/app.js\" defer></script></body></html>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
